---
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeaderV7.astro";
import SiteMediaLoader from "../components/SiteMediaLoader.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Privacy | HarborNavi</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="How HarborNavi handles launch-list email, Pilot Families applications, campaign analytics, and 15 Homes application data."
    />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" type="image/png" sizes="512x512" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://harbornavi.com/privacy" />
  </head>
  <body data-route="privacy">
    <SiteHeader />
    <main>
      <section class="privacy-page section-shell">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>How the HarborNavi website handles your information.</h1>
        <p>
          This page explains the current public data flows for the HarborNavi launch list, first-party campaign
          analytics, Pilot Families applications, and 15 Homes Across America. The website signup flow is separate from the planned local-first
          product data path.
        </p>
        <div class="privacy-grid">
          <article>
            <h2>Current launch page</h2>
            <p>
              <code>/home-v6</code> is the current launch page. <code>/</code> and <code>/home</code> redirect there.
              <code>/home-v4</code> and <code>/home-v5</code> are no-index historical comparisons; their signup forms
              are inactive and point visitors to the current page.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Waitlist submission</h2>
            <p>
              Submitting a V6 or V7 waitlist form saves the normalized email address, source and attribution fields,
              consent time, and operational status in the Neon Postgres <code>waitlist_leads</code> table. The address
              joins the HarborNavi waitlist immediately.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>No confirmation step</h2>
            <p>
              HarborNavi does not require a confirmation link after submission. The form clearly states that submitting
              joins the waitlist and may result in HarborNavi product and Kickstarter pre-launch updates.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Subscriber connection</h2>
            <p>
              After the database save, the address is synced to one Resend Topic for HarborNavi Kickstarter pre-launch
              updates. A temporary provider failure does not remove the address from the waitlist; the sync is retried.
              Every campaign message includes the provider's unsubscribe control.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Operational status</h2>
            <p>
              Consent time, Resend contact sync, and operator-notification status are kept in
              <code>waitlist_leads.metadata</code>. An authenticated scheduled job retries eligible integration failures
              and initializes the Kickstarter Topic when an override ID is not configured.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
            <p>
              A waitlist lead remains in Neon until a deletion request is received. Email
              <a href="mailto:waitlist@harbornavi.com">waitlist@harbornavi.com</a> to request deletion. A campaign
              unsubscribe stops campaign delivery but does not by itself delete the Neon lead record.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Campaign email and alerts</h2>
            <p>
              Kickstarter updates are sent as reviewed Resend Broadcasts with the provider's unsubscribe mechanism.
              After submission, HarborNavi also sends an operator alert so the lead can be handled. Provider failures
              are retried without requiring the visitor to submit again.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Optional product research survey</h2>
            <p>
              After a V6 submission, HarborNavi may offer a voluntary product survey hosted by SurveyMonkey. It may ask
              for an age range, occupation, smart-home use, current devices, and product preferences. SurveyMonkey
              processes the response and related technical data under its own privacy terms; HarborNavi uses received
              answers for compatibility research and product priorities. Survey answers are separate from launch-list
              consent and are not written to this site's Neon waitlist or analytics tables. Do not provide an address,
              account or camera credentials, raw media, or sensitive household details. Responses are retained for the
              active product-research cycle and can be deleted earlier by emailing waitlist@harbornavi.com.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Campaign analytics</h2>
            <p>
              First-party campaign analytics records page and link events with route, session, and attribution data.
              Email addresses, application answers, postal details, camera models, and household details are not sent
              as analytics event properties.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Pilot Families application</h2>
            <p>
              The Pilot Families form collects name, email, ZIP Code, a high-level smart-device summary, interest in the
              program, and referral source. Applications are stored in Neon for selection and pilot operations and do not
              create a marketing subscription. Do not submit passwords, camera credentials, raw footage, a full street
              address, or sensitive household details. Applications that are not selected are removed within 12 months
              after pilot selection closes; selected-family records are retained for the active pilot and related support.
              An applicant may request earlier deletion through the contact address used for pilot communication. During
              the pilot, household camera footage, device credentials, and the private home timeline remain local to the
              HarborNavi device. Participants choose what feedback, vlog footage, and optional diagnostics to share.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>15 Homes application</h2>
            <p>
              The host application is an external form. It may ask for contact details, metro area, availability, a
              high-level device or home-system summary, and readiness for a visit. Do not submit raw footage, camera
              credentials, or a full street address during initial screening. The form stays disabled until its provider,
              retention window, deletion-request contact, and applicant information are published on the active surface.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Product direction</h2>
            <p>
              HarborNavi is being designed for local-first home intelligence. The launch-list flow described here does
              not collect raw home video, camera credentials, or device telemetry. Material changes to these public
              flows should be reflected on this page before collection begins.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p>
          To stop campaign email, use the unsubscribe control in a Broadcast. To request deletion of a launch-list
          address, email <a href="mailto:waitlist@harbornavi.com">waitlist@harbornavi.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer">
      <span>HarborNavi</span>
      <a href="/home">Home</a>
    </footer>
    <SiteMediaLoader />
  </body>
</html>
